WEBVTT

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:09.808
[squeaks]

00:00:09.852 --> 00:00:12.898
Welcome home.

00:00:12.942 --> 00:00:15.249
[choir singing]

00:00:15.292 --> 00:00:18.817
[music distorting]

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.345
-[coughs, pops]
-[gasps]

00:00:24.388 --> 00:00:25.259
[squeaking]

00:00:25.302 --> 00:00:26.999
Oh, Mr. Dinkles, you're alive.

00:00:27.043 --> 00:00:29.219
For a minute there, I thought
you'd kicked the bucket.

00:00:29.263 --> 00:00:31.134
[groans]

00:00:31.178 --> 00:00:34.659
[Poppy and Branch
coughing, panting]

00:00:34.703 --> 00:00:36.661
I'm really glad
you came with me.

00:00:36.705 --> 00:00:38.533
[panting]

00:00:38.576 --> 00:00:39.621
-Me, too.
-[galloping]

00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:40.926
HICKORY:
Yah!

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.232
There you are. Whew!

00:00:42.276 --> 00:00:43.755
-I think we lost them.
-[grunting]

00:00:43.799 --> 00:00:45.409
-We should be all right.
-Thank you.

00:00:45.453 --> 00:00:47.585
I don't know
how we can ever repay you.

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:49.413
Oh, wait! Yes, I do.

00:00:49.457 --> 00:00:50.458
Gumdrops!

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:51.807
Gum what?

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.244
Oh. Well, thank you.

00:00:54.288 --> 00:00:56.159
Whew. That's got a zing,
don't it?

00:00:56.203 --> 00:00:58.117
-Uh... Whoa.
-It's not candy time.

00:00:58.161 --> 00:00:59.554
It's question time.

00:00:59.597 --> 00:01:00.555
-[bell dings]
-Huh?

00:01:00.598 --> 00:01:01.904
-Hug time!
-Hug time!

00:01:01.947 --> 00:01:03.775
-Ooh. Oh, that feels good.
-Wow.

00:01:03.819 --> 00:01:05.429
[grunts]

00:01:05.473 --> 00:01:08.127
-Why are you helping us?
-[bell dings]

00:01:08.171 --> 00:01:09.781
What's in it for you?

00:01:09.825 --> 00:01:11.043
Hey! Branch.

00:01:11.087 --> 00:01:14.786
[chuckles] I'm sorry
about my... associate.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:16.266
HICKORY:
I loved your message about

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.876
music bringing Trolls together.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.533
You may be Pop, and I may be
Country, but Trolls is Trolls.

00:01:22.577 --> 00:01:24.274
[imitates Hickory]:
"Trolls is Trolls."

00:01:24.318 --> 00:01:25.710
Wow. Deep.

00:01:25.754 --> 00:01:28.452
This is the beginning of
a partnership between Trolls

00:01:28.496 --> 00:01:30.933
that's going to save
all Trolls.

00:01:30.976 --> 00:01:32.282
You're darn skippy.

00:01:32.326 --> 00:01:33.762
-[chuckles]: Ah.
-[groans]

00:01:33.805 --> 00:01:36.591
Okay. We need to get to
the Funk Trolls before Barb.

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:38.593
HICKORY: Well, quickest way
is down that river.

00:01:38.636 --> 00:01:40.769
I'll build us a raft.

00:01:40.812 --> 00:01:42.161
[scoffs]
This ought to be good.

00:01:42.205 --> 00:01:43.293
Guy probably doesn't know

00:01:43.337 --> 00:01:45.121
the first thing about
building a ra...

00:01:48.516 --> 00:01:50.779
Cappuccino, anyone?

00:01:50.822 --> 00:01:51.780
Cappuccino?

00:01:51.823 --> 00:01:53.172
Cappucci-yes.

00:01:53.216 --> 00:01:55.000
-Oh!
-Are you seeing this?

00:01:55.044 --> 00:01:56.219
BIGGIE:
Oh, wow.

00:01:56.263 --> 00:01:57.829
[sighs] I do want one.

00:01:57.873 --> 00:01:59.875
But I am not happy about it.

00:02:03.618 --> 00:02:06.185
[gasping]

00:02:07.665 --> 00:02:09.363
Trolls that look like me!

00:02:09.406 --> 00:02:10.364
Yes!

00:02:10.407 --> 00:02:11.626
[giggles]

00:02:14.193 --> 00:02:14.933
Oh.

00:02:14.977 --> 00:02:16.674
[clucking]

00:02:16.718 --> 00:02:19.373
[purring]

00:02:21.244 --> 00:02:23.681
-Hello there.
-[sniffs]

00:02:23.725 --> 00:02:26.336
-[honking musically]
-[funky beat playing]

00:02:28.556 --> 00:02:30.209
[grunts]

00:02:30.253 --> 00:02:31.559
-[screams]
-[music stops]

00:02:34.692 --> 00:02:37.129
Happy birthday?

00:02:39.218 --> 00:02:42.526
HICKORY: I can make a cortado,
a macchiato, latte.

00:02:44.006 --> 00:02:45.660
-We also do drip.
-BIGGIE: Oh.

00:02:45.703 --> 00:02:47.052
It is a nice night, isn't it?

00:02:47.096 --> 00:02:48.358
Mr. Dinkles loves a full moon.

00:02:48.402 --> 00:02:50.708
-Let's get our grub on.
-[sighs]

00:02:50.752 --> 00:02:52.101
Food's ready.

00:02:52.144 --> 00:02:53.537
[Southern accent]:
Well, I'll bring more kindlin'.

00:02:53.581 --> 00:02:55.104
Poppy, maybe it's just me,

00:02:55.147 --> 00:02:57.367
but are you getting
a weird vibe from Hickory?

00:02:57.411 --> 00:02:58.542
[normal voice]:
What?

00:02:58.586 --> 00:02:59.717
No. Why? Are you?

00:02:59.761 --> 00:03:01.197
I just-- I don't know.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.503
-I don't trust him.
-BIGGIE: Oh, that's good.

00:03:02.546 --> 00:03:03.721
POPPY:
Well, yeah, but you don't

00:03:03.765 --> 00:03:05.070
-trust anybody, Branch.
-[grub squeaking]

00:03:05.114 --> 00:03:07.029
Hey, I just want us to be safe.

00:03:07.072 --> 00:03:08.465
And you know what's not safe?

00:03:08.509 --> 00:03:10.946
Putting too much trust
into a complete stranger.

00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:13.078
Oh, I see.

00:03:13.122 --> 00:03:15.951
It's not Hickory
you don't trust. It's me.

00:03:16.908 --> 00:03:18.519
Do you not think
I'm a good queen?

00:03:18.562 --> 00:03:20.390
Wait, what?
I didn't say that.

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:21.957
I thought we were friends,
Branch.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.741
I'm starting to think you don't
even know what that means.

00:03:23.785 --> 00:03:25.264
We arefriends.

00:03:25.308 --> 00:03:26.788
And sometimes
that means speaking up

00:03:26.831 --> 00:03:29.530
if I think
you're making a mistake.

00:03:29.573 --> 00:03:32.315
-[smooth jazz music playing]
-Do you hear something?

00:03:36.711 --> 00:03:39.714
[chuckles]
Look at that guy's chest hair.

00:03:39.757 --> 00:03:40.889
[distorted sigh]

00:03:40.932 --> 00:03:43.239
BRANCH:
Poppy,

00:03:43.282 --> 00:03:46.242
[distorted]:
I can't feel my face.

00:03:46.285 --> 00:03:50.115
It's... it's like
I'm being paralyzed by its

00:03:50.159 --> 00:03:52.117
[echoes]:
smoothness.

00:03:52.161 --> 00:03:54.381
[smooth jazz music continues]

00:03:57.645 --> 00:03:58.602
[roars]

00:03:58.646 --> 00:04:00.299
[bubbles fizzing]

00:04:02.954 --> 00:04:04.478
[phone ringing]

00:04:06.001 --> 00:04:07.132
[distorted]:
Hello?

00:04:07.176 --> 00:04:09.004
Hello. It's me.

00:04:09.047 --> 00:04:10.005
[laughs]

00:04:10.048 --> 00:04:12.311
Look! Narwhals.

00:04:12.355 --> 00:04:15.314
-POPPY: Totally gnar-gnar.
-[narwhals whistling]

00:04:15.358 --> 00:04:17.404
BIGGIE [in distance]:
Poppy!

00:04:18.666 --> 00:04:20.624
[giggling]

00:04:20.668 --> 00:04:21.669
Oh.

00:04:24.323 --> 00:04:25.281
-[music stops]
-Ah...

00:04:25.324 --> 00:04:26.761
BRANCH:
Poppy,

00:04:26.804 --> 00:04:29.198
how'd you like the sushi?

00:04:29.241 --> 00:04:30.591
-[groaning]
-Oh.

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.506
-CHAZ: Got you, Pop babies.
-[gasps]

00:04:32.549 --> 00:04:35.465
Soon, Barb is gonna
have your string,

00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:39.643
and the world will be rid of
cheesy, pointless pop music,

00:04:39.687 --> 00:04:41.253
once and for all.

00:04:41.297 --> 00:04:43.821
Hold it right there, Chaz.

00:04:43.865 --> 00:04:48.086
And who are you supposed to be,
cowboy pants?

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.566
-[Trolls gasp]
-My name's Hickory,

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.830
and I don't much care
for smooth jazz.

00:04:52.874 --> 00:04:54.223
-[Trolls gasp]
-Oh, yeah?

00:04:54.266 --> 00:04:58.923
Well, you've just never had
the Chaz experience.

00:04:58.967 --> 00:05:00.534
[smooth jazz music playing]

00:05:03.537 --> 00:05:05.843
-[music stops]
-Ooh. Ah.

00:05:05.887 --> 00:05:07.018
[saxophone honks]

00:05:07.062 --> 00:05:08.019
[ears pop softly]

00:05:08.063 --> 00:05:09.368
Gumdrops.

00:05:09.412 --> 00:05:12.067
Soundproof and delicious.

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:14.809
Smooth jazz
will be heard again!

00:05:14.852 --> 00:05:18.203
Smooth jazz will never die!

00:05:18.247 --> 00:05:19.727
[blows note]

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.511
Who was that guy?

00:05:21.555 --> 00:05:24.209
One of the many bounty hunters
out there looking for you.

00:05:24.253 --> 00:05:26.168
That was awful.

00:05:26.211 --> 00:05:28.213
So smooth and easy and awful.

00:05:28.257 --> 00:05:29.693
I know, big buddy.

00:05:29.737 --> 00:05:31.782
It's enough to put you
off jazz altogether.

00:05:31.826 --> 00:05:34.393
BIGGIE: All right, that's it!
We need to go home.

00:05:34.437 --> 00:05:35.612
Biggie, it'll be okay.

00:05:35.656 --> 00:05:37.527
Stop saying that,
and listen to me.

00:05:37.571 --> 00:05:40.138
You only hear
what you want to hear,

00:05:40.182 --> 00:05:41.531
and it puts us all in danger.

00:05:41.575 --> 00:05:43.925
How are you supposed
to save the world

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:45.796
if you can't even keep us safe?

00:05:47.276 --> 00:05:50.671
You made a pinky promise to me,
Queen Poppy.

00:05:50.714 --> 00:05:52.455
And you broke it.

00:05:58.592 --> 00:06:00.594
[blabbering rapidly]

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:10.299
What kind of queen
breaks a pinky promise?!

00:06:11.126 --> 00:06:13.041
Biggie.

00:06:13.084 --> 00:06:14.477
No.

00:06:15.913 --> 00:06:17.872
[sizzling]

00:06:17.915 --> 00:06:20.135
♪

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:25.836
[panting]

00:06:28.491 --> 00:06:30.101
[wheezing]:
I'm so lost.

00:06:30.145 --> 00:06:31.799
I'm almost there.
I'm so lost.

00:06:31.842 --> 00:06:34.497
So hot.

00:06:34.541 --> 00:06:35.977
[coughs]

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.239
[gasps]

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:43.201
♪

00:06:43.245 --> 00:06:45.508
[gasps]

00:06:46.814 --> 00:06:48.729
[gasps] I'm saved!

00:06:48.772 --> 00:06:50.774
[gulping]

00:06:50.818 --> 00:06:52.602
Are you, now?

00:06:52.646 --> 00:06:56.214
'Cause last I checked,
I was a mirage.

00:06:56.258 --> 00:06:58.652
[echoing]:
...a mirage, a mirage.

00:06:59.653 --> 00:07:01.611
[groaning]

00:07:05.136 --> 00:07:06.311
[sobs]

00:07:06.355 --> 00:07:08.139
I'm done for.

00:07:08.183 --> 00:07:12.709
And on top of that, I never
found any Trolls like me.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.716
[electronic humming
and pulsing]

